  m_Name: 1299
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Founding of Singapura 1299 '
  info: According to the Malay Annals, Prince Sang Nila Utama, a ruler from Palembang,
    is said to have arrived on the island while searching for a new settlement. Upon
    reportedly seeing a lion (though likely a tiger), he names the island "Singapura,"
    meaning "Lion City." This event symbolizes the establishment of the island as
    a significant port and royal outpost. Singapura becomes a small but thriving
    trading center, attracting regional traders and sailors.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cce8898b6e8aa4da6bb90f5e956f42e7, type: 3}
